Root
  Tool: Commercial, open-source, built-in, or publicly available software that could be used by a defender, pen tester, red teamer, or an adversary. This category includes both software that generally is not found on an enterprise system as well as software generally available as part of an operating system that is already present in an environment. Examples include PsExec, Metasploit, Mimikatz, as well as Windows utilities such as Net, netstat, Tasklist, etc.
    Built-in System Utilities - Native operating system tools and commands
      ~Net Commands (net.exe, net1.exe) - Network and user account management
      ~PowerShell - Scripting and automation shell
      ~Windows Management Instrumentation (WMIC) - System management
      ~Task Scheduler (schtasks.exe) - Task automation and scheduling
      ~Registry Editor Tools (reg.exe, regedit.exe) - Registry manipulation
      ~Command Prompt (cmd.exe) - Command-line interface
      ~System Information Tools (systeminfo.exe, msinfo32.exe) - System details gathering
      ~Windows Credential Manager (cmdkey.exe) - Credential management
      ~Service Control Manager (sc.exe) - Service management
      ~Remote Desktop Tools (mstsc.exe) - Remote system access
      ~Query Commands (query.exe) - Session and process information
      ~Bash Shell (/bin/bash) - Unix command interpreter
      ~Task Manager Tools (tasklist.exe, taskkill.exe) - Process management
      ~Windows Certificate Tools (certutil.exe) - Certificate and encoding utilities
      ~Network Commands (netstat.exe, route.exe) - Network configuration
      ~Event Viewer Tools (wevtutil.exe) - Log management
      ~Volume Shadow Copy Tools (vssadmin.exe) - Backup management
      ~Windows Debug Tools (debug.exe) - Binary examination
      ~Directory Services Tools (dsquery.exe, dsget.exe) - Active Directory queries
      ~Resource Kit Utilities (robocopy.exe, move.exe) - File operations
      ~Group Policy Tools (gpupdate.exe, gpresult.exe) - Policy management
      ~Unix System Commands (sudo, su) - Privilege management
      ~Windows Performance Tools (perfmon.exe) - System monitoring
      ~Archive Commands (tar, zip, compress) - File compression
      ~Mount Commands (mount.exe, mountvol.exe) - Volume management
      ~Remote Shell Tools (rsh, ssh) - Remote access
      ~DNS Tools (nslookup.exe, dnscmd.exe) - DNS management
      ~Windows Scripting Host (wscript.exe, cscript.exe) - Script execution
