    Protocol Analysis Tools - Specialized tools for analyzing network protocols
      ~Use Wireshark to capture and analyze unencrypted credentials and sensitive data from network traffic, focusing on protocols like HTTP, FTP, and SMTP
      ~Deploy Tcpdump on compromised systems to monitor and log network communications, capturing packet data for offline analysis
      ~Utilize Burp Suite to intercept and modify web application traffic, testing for vulnerabilities and manipulating requests
      ~Employ NetworkMiner for passive network surveillance, extracting files, credentials, and metadata from captured traffic
      ~Use Ettercap for ARP poisoning and MITM attacks, intercepting traffic between network hosts
      ~Deploy Fiddler to analyze HTTPS traffic by installing custom certificates and decrypting SSL/TLS communications
      ~Utilize Nmap with protocol-specific NSE scripts to identify and analyze services running on target systems
      ~Use Scapy to craft custom packets for protocol analysis and network manipulation
      ~Deploy SmartSniff for quick network monitoring on Windows systems without installation requirements
      ~Use Microsoft Message Analyzer to capture and analyze Windows-specific network protocols and events
      ~Use Aircrack-ng suite for analyzing and attacking wireless network protocols (WEP/WPA/WPA2)
      ~Deploy Proxify to intercept and analyze non-HTTP protocol traffic like MQTT, AMQP, and custom protocols
      ~Utilize Modbus Scanner for analyzing industrial control system protocols and identifying vulnerable devices
      ~Use Omnipeek for real-time analysis of VoIP protocols (SIP, RTP) and call monitoring
      ~Deploy Zeek (formerly Bro) for large-scale protocol analysis and network security monitoring
      ~Use SIPVicious suite for analyzing and exploiting VoIP/SIP protocols in telephony systems
      ~Utilize CAN Bus analyzer tools for intercepting and analyzing automotive network protocols
      ~Deploy Sylvester for analyzing proprietary protocols through pattern recognition and reverse engineering
      ~Use Echo Mirage for intercepting and modifying thick client application protocols
      ~Deploy SocketSniff for analyzing Windows socket communications in specific applications
      ~Use Responder to analyze and exploit LLMNR/NBT-NS/MDNS protocols for credential capture
      ~Deploy tshark for automated protocol analysis and data extraction through command-line scripting
      ~Utilize Cain & Abel for analyzing authentication protocols and performing protocol-specific MITM attacks
      ~Use RITA (Real Intelligence Threat Analytics) for analyzing DNS and other protocol patterns at scale
      ~Deploy Protocol Buffers decoder tools for analyzing and manipulating gRPC communications
      ~Use SQLMap's traffic analysis features for intercepting and analyzing database protocol communications
      ~Utilize CloudShark for collaborative analysis of captured protocol traffic in cloud environments
      ~Deploy SSLsplit for analyzing and intercepting SSL/TLS protocols in non-standard implementations
      ~Use Intercepter-NG for analyzing multiple network protocols simultaneously on various platforms
      ~Deploy ProtocolDetective for identifying and analyzing unknown protocols through behavior analysis
