  Malware: Commercial, custom closed source, or open source software intended to be used for malicious purposes by adversaries. Examples include PlugX, CHOPSTICK, etc.
    Remote Access Trojans (RATs): Malware designed to provide unauthorized remote access and control
      ~PlugX: Modular RAT commonly used in targeted attacks with plugin architecture
      ~Poison Ivy: Classic RAT with encrypted C2, file operations, and keylogging capabilities
      ~njRAT: Arabic-language RAT with remote desktop, keylogging, and webcam control
      ~DarkComet: Feature-rich RAT with remote desktop, file management, and keylogging
      ~Gh0st RAT: Chinese-origin RAT with remote control and data exfiltration capabilities
      ~QuasarRAT: Open-source .NET-based RAT with extensive remote control features
      ~jRAT: Java-based cross-platform RAT with plugin support and stealth capabilities
      ~NetWire: Commercial RAT with remote desktop, file transfer, and keylogging
      ~Remcos: Commercial RAT marketed as remote administration tool with extensive features
      ~XtremeRAT: Feature-rich RAT with remote shell, file management, and process control
      ~Havex: Industrial control system targeted RAT used in energy sector attacks
      ~AdWind/JBifrost: Cross-platform Java RAT with multiple variants and aliases
      ~LuminosityLink: RAT with built-in evasion and cryptocurrency mining capabilities
      ~NanoCore: Modular RAT with extensive plugin system and builder functionality
      ~CobianRAT: RAT with ransomware capabilities and sophisticated C2 infrastructure
      ~Imminent Monitor: Previously commercial RAT with advanced surveillance features
      ~Orcus RAT: Marketed as legitimate remote administration tool but used maliciously
      ~AsyncRAT: Open-source .NET RAT with encrypted communications
      ~RevengeRAT: Feature-rich RAT with robust data stealing capabilities
      ~BlackShades: Notorious RAT known for mass-market distribution
      ~Warzone RAT (Ave Maria): Modern RAT with advanced evasion and anti-analysis features
      ~FlawedAmmyy: RAT based on leaked Ammyy Admin source code
