    Macro Malware: Malware that leverages document macro capabilities
      ~Create malicious VBA macros in Office documents that execute PowerShell commands to download and run additional payloads
      ~Implement Auto_Open/AutoExec macros that trigger automatically when documents are opened
      ~Use macro obfuscation techniques like string splitting, encoding, and dead code insertion to evade detection
      ~Abuse legitimate Office functions (e.g., AutoOpen, Document_Open) to establish persistence
      ~Employ social engineering tactics to convince users to enable macros (e.g., fake document protection notices)
      ~Utilize COM objects within macros to interact with Windows APIs and execute system commands
      ~Implement macro code to check for virtualization/sandbox environments before executing payload
      ~Create macros that leverage DDE (Dynamic Data Exchange) for code execution
      ~Use macro stomping techniques to hide malicious code in document properties
      ~Deploy macros that establish encrypted communication channels with C2 servers
