      ~Create self-replicating macros that infect other Office documents on the system
      ~Use macro code to disable security features like Protected View and Trust Center settings
      ~Implement multi-stage macro execution where initial macro downloads encrypted secondary stages
      ~Create macros that leverage Windows Management Instrumentation (WMI) for system reconnaissance
      ~Use macro code to modify registry keys for Office security settings
      ~Deploy macros that leverage alternate data streams (ADS) to hide payload components
