    Cloud Service Malware: Malware designed to exploit cloud services and infrastructure
      ~Deploy malware that exploits AWS API credentials through metadata service endpoints to gain initial access and establish persistence
      ~Utilize Azure AD backdoors to maintain persistent access and conduct privilege escalation across cloud resources
      ~Implement cloud storage-based C2 channels using S3 buckets or Azure Blob storage for covert communication
      ~Exploit container orchestration platforms (Kubernetes) to spread malware across cloud-native applications
