      ~Create backdoor OAuth applications to maintain persistent access to cloud services and data
      ~Utilize cloud function serverless environments for malware execution and lateral movement
      ~Exploit cloud identity federation services to pivot across multiple cloud accounts and organizations
      ~Deploy malware that targets cloud-based CI/CD pipelines to inject malicious code into production systems
      ~Implement cloud logging service exploits to hide malicious activity and maintain stealth
      ~Exploit cloud-managed database services (RDS, CosmosDB) to exfiltrate data and maintain persistence through malicious stored procedures
      ~Abuse cloud messaging services (SQS, Service Bus) for distributed command and control infrastructure
      ~Manipulate cloud backup systems and snapshots to maintain persistence and hide malicious artifacts
      ~Deploy malware that targets virtual network infrastructure (VPCs, VNets) to intercept and manipulate cloud traffic
      ~Implement malware that bypasses cloud WAF and DDoS protection services through protocol manipulation
      ~Exploit cloud load balancers and application gateways to distribute malware across cloud regions
      ~Target cloud DNS services to redirect traffic and establish covert communication channels
